# 🚀 Day 51 – Product Discovery & Sprint Planning

> **10-Day Capstone Kickoff | From Idea to Deployed v1.0**

## 📌 Overview

Welcome to **Day 51** of the **AB Talks 60-Day Claude AI Challenge**!

Today marks the beginning of the **10-Day Capstone Project**, where the focus shifts from building individual AI applications to developing and shipping a complete, production-ready product by following a structured **Software Development Lifecycle (SDLC).**

Rather than writing code immediately, today's objective was to establish a strong foundation through **Product Discovery, Requirement Analysis, Scope Definition, and Sprint Planning**. Every decision made today will guide the remaining nine days of development and ensure the project remains realistic, focused, and deliverable within the timeline.

---

# 🎯 Goal

Transform a product idea into a clear execution plan that can be successfully designed, built, tested, deployed, and demonstrated within **10 days**.

---

# 🛠 Software Development Lifecycle

The capstone follows a complete SDLC approach:

```text
Requirements
      │
      ▼
Product Discovery
      │
      ▼
Sprint Planning
      │
      ▼
System Design
      │
      ▼
Implementation
      │
      ▼
Testing
      │
      ▼
Deployment
      │
      ▼
Maintenance
```

---

# 📋 Day 51 Objectives

* Discover the right product idea
* Validate the problem to solve
* Identify target users
* Define MVP scope
* Prevent scope creep
* Create a realistic implementation roadmap
* Plan daily milestones
* Define project success criteria

---

# 📦 Deliverables

## 1️⃣ Product Requirements Document (PRD)

A comprehensive PRD covering:

* Product Vision
* Problem Statement
* Target Users
* Goals & Objectives
* User Stories
* Functional Requirements
* Non-Functional Requirements
* MVP Definition
* Risks & Assumptions
* Success Metrics

---

## 2️⃣ Implementation Blueprint (Days 2–10)

A detailed day-by-day development plan including:

* 🎯 Daily Objectives
* 📖 Learning Goals
* 🛠 Features to Build
* 📝 Step-by-Step Implementation
* 📂 Files & Folder Structure
* 🔗 Required Integrations
* 🧪 Testing Tasks
* 🐞 Debugging Tips
* ✅ Daily Checklist
* 📸 Expected Progress
* ➡️ Handoff Notes

This blueprint serves as the **single source of truth** for the remainder of the capstone.

---

## 3️⃣ Product Pitch Deck

A presentation-ready deck covering:

* Problem
* Target Users
* Solution
* Value Proposition
* Key Features
* Technical Vision
* Future Scope
* Long-Term Product Strategy

